        96.0355453491211
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "there are two sources of errors: 1) the ensemble score",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        95.25836181640625,
        541.4371337890625,
        104.16492462158203
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "approximation ∇log pt ≈sN, and 2) the initial distribution",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        106.24700164794922,
        541.435546875,
        125.02710723876953
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "approximation pT ≈πref due to finite time horizon T. For",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        118.20195770263672,
        541.6092529296875,
        136.98207092285156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "clarity, we here focus on continuous-time analysis, although",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        131.12335205078125,
        541.4381713867188,
        140.0299072265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "discretisation errors may be considered within a similar",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        143.079345703125,
        541.6099243164062,
        151.98590087890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "framework (see e.g., Lord et al., 2014). We aim to analyse",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        155.03436279296875,
        541.4370727539062,
        163.94091796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the geometric distance between the resampling distribution",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        166.9893798828125,
        541.4414672851562,
        175.89593505859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "eqt and the target π under these errors in relation to t and N.",
      "bbox": [
        307.4477233886719,
        178.78492736816406,
        543.1622314453125,
        191.67652893066406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Unless otherwise needed, for any parameter T > 0 we",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        196.7179718017578,
        541.440673828125,
        205.783935546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "assume the usual textbook linear growth and Lipschitz con-",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        208.83233642578125,
        543.0975341796875,
        217.7388916015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ditions on X and U so that a strong solution exists and",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        220.62794494628906,
        541.4429931640625,
        229.69390869140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "R t",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        227.68215942382812,
        317.0946960449219,
        238.49952697753906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "0|X(τ)| dτ has finite variance, see, for instance, Karatzas",
      "bbox": [
        312.1449890136719,
        232.825927734375,
        541.4376831054688,
        250.1110382080078
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "& Shreve (1991, pp. 289) or Øksendal (2007, Thm. 5.2.1).",
      "bbox": [
        307.052001953125,
        245.74835205078125,
        543.1844482421875,
        254.6549072265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "This also ensures a smooth transition density pt|τ for all",
      "bbox": [
        307.1310119628906,
        257.5439758300781,
        541.4383544921875,
        268.408935546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "0 ≤τ < t ≤T so that the ensemble score sN and its gradi-",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        268.6920166015625,
        543.0931396484375,
        285.97711181640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ent in Equation (6) are pointwise well defined. We also as-",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        281.6133728027344,
        543.0894775390625,
        290.5199279785156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "sume the existence of the reverse process in the sense of An-",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        293.568359375,
        543.0980224609375,
        302.47491455078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "derson (1982), i.e., the reversal solves the same Kolmogorov",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        305.52337646484375,
        541.6920776367188,
        314.429931640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "forward equation in reverse time, although the established",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        317.4793701171875,
        541.4429321289062,
        326.38592529296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "conditions for this are still implicit (see, e.g., Haussmann",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        329.4343566894531,
        541.4370727539062,
        338.3409118652344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "& Pardoux, 1986; Millet et al., 1989). Denote the Wasser-",
      "bbox": [
        307.052001953125,
        341.3893737792969,
        543.091552734375,
        350.2959289550781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "stein distance by Wl",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        351.6441955566406,
        391.06854248046875,
        362.25091552734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "l(p, q) = inf γ∈Γ(p,q) E[|X −Y |l] for",
      "bbox": [
        388.4119873046875,
        351.64422607421875,
        541.6097412109375,
        369.6631164550781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(X, Y ) ∼γ, where Γ is the set of all couplings of (p, q).",
      "bbox": [
        306.2749938964844,
        364.3329772949219,
        543.1834716796875,
        381.6180725097656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We say a distribution ν is z-strongly log-concave if",
      "bbox": [
        306.97198486328125,
        377.094970703125,
        511.0458068847656,
        386.1609191894531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "∇log ν(x) −∇log ν(x′), x −x′",
      "bbox": [
        326.28399658203125,
        396.4486389160156,
        460.40435791015625,
        415.3560791015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "≤−z |x −x′|2,",
      "bbox": [
        463.1730041503906,
        396.4486389160156,
        527.3035888671875,
        415.3560791015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and we denote it by ν ⪯z. The assumptions that we",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        419.85400390625,
        541.43798828125,
        437.13909912109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "globally use are as follows.",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        432.7763671875,
        415.9327087402344,
        441.68292236328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Assumption 1 (Diffusion conditions). There exist positive",
      "bbox": [
        307.0820007324219,
        448.54278564453125,
        541.4420776367188,
        457.56890869140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "constants 2 Cp < Cref < 2 C−",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        457.8796691894531,
        430.506591796875,
        470.7987365722656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ref + 2 Cp such that",
      "bbox": [
        423.5669860839844,
        460.4579772949219,
        502.8864440917969,
        472.30975341796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "∇log πref(x) −∇log πref(x′)",
      "bbox": [
        328.0469970703125,
        481.23065185546875,
        450.60748291015625,
        500.13909912109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "≤Cref |x −x′|,",
      "bbox": [
        450.60601806640625,
        480.3630065917969,
        520.8381958007812,
        501.6330871582031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for all x, x′ ∈Rd, πref ⪯C−",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        502.5899963378906,
        425.380615234375,
        524.985107421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ref, and pt ⪯Cp for all t ≥0.",
      "bbox": [
        418.4410095214844,
        506.20599365234375,
        538.543701171875,
        524.985107421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Assumption 2 (Ensemble score condition). There exist a",
      "bbox": [
        307.0820007324219,
        522.9387817382812,
        541.4450073242188,
        531.9649047851562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "constant r > 0 and a positive non-increasing smooth func-",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        534.8539428710938,
        543.097900390625,
        543.7007446289062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tion t 7→Ce(t), such that",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        546.0020141601562,
        408.35919189453125,
        563.287109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "sup",
      "bbox": [
        330.6190185546875,
        574.3359375,
        345.6227111816406,
        583.1827392578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "x∈Rd E",
      "bbox": [
        329.3960266113281,
        576.6273803710938,
        356.80706787109375,
        591.6519165039062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\u0002",
      "bbox": [
        356.80401611328125,
        572.781494140625,
        360.95843505859375,
        579.1575317382812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "|∇log pt(x) −sN(x, t)|2\u00031/2 ≤Ce(t)",
      "bbox": [
        360.95501708984375,
        567.5239868164062,
        515.5223999023438,
        590.8140869140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "N r .",
      "bbox": [
        497.39801025390625,
        574.3359375,
        519.4866333007812,
        590.0167236328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for all t > 0, where E takes on the weighted samples.",
      "bbox": [
        307.4400634765625,
        602.596923828125,
        520.0518798828125,
        611.4437255859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Recall that the ensemble score defined in Equation (6) is",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        624.620361328125,
        541.4409790039062,
        633.5269165039062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "exactly a self-normalised importance sampling, where π is",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        636.4159545898438,
        541.4400024414062,
        645.48193359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the proposal, π(x0 | xt) ∝pt|0(xt | x0) π(x0) is the target,",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        647.5640258789062,
        542.6848754882812,
        666.3430786132812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and ∇log pt|0(xt | x0) is the test function. The condition",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        659.5189819335938,
        541.4446411132812,
        678.298095703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in Assumption 2 is thus akin to non-asymptotic variance",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        672.4403686523438,
        541.43701171875,
        681.346923828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "bounds of importance sampling, and this has been well es-",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        684.3953857421875,
        543.0908203125,
        693.3019409179688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tablished by, for example, Agapiou et al. (2017) and Chopin",
      "bbox": [
        307.44000244140625,
        696.3513793945312,
        541.438232421875,
        705.2579345703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "& Papaspiliopoulos (2020, Thm. 8.5). Typically, the Monte",
      "bbox": [
        307.052001953125,
        708.3063354492188,
        541.4443969726562,
        717.212890625
      ],
      "direction": [
